  "result": "Milestones are implemented as specified. The full suite passes (630 tests, including 13 new ones in `tests/services/milestone-service.test.ts`), and type-check and lint are clean.\n\nI updated the visible tests and fixtures that build an `Issue` or an issue input so they include `milestoneId: null`. Existing databases also get the new `milestone_id` column on issues when migrations run; I checked that against an old-style database, running the migration twice.\n\nBehaviour the spec didn't pin down, so you know what I chose:\n- **Name spacing:** names are stored with surrounding spaces trimmed, so `\"  Beta \"` is saved as `\"Beta\"`.\n- **Extra event:** moving an issue into or out of a milestone also publishes `issue.updated` (with `milestoneId` as the changed field), like other issue edits. Setting the milestone an issue already has publishes nothing.\n- **Closed milestones:** they can still be renamed and re-dated.",
